# Line endings are LF in the index and LF in every working tree, whatever a
# machine's core.autocrlf says. Windows is the reason: a checkout there would
# otherwise hold CRLF, and three things in this repository read bytes rather
# than lines. The packed skills under tools/ are compared byte for byte with
# their source markdown; the shell suites and the git hooks are run by bash,
# which refuses a script whose lines end in CR; and the digest a spec change
# is measured by is a hash of the file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so neither the index nor a checkout ever rewrites a byte.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
